## v1.1.3b1 — 2026-11-25

Changes since v1.1.2b1 (beta):

+ Add `add-secret` and `update-runner --secret` to import Kerberos keytabs into
  Yuki and bind them to REANA or SSH runners. Credentials remain outside project
  configuration and impressions. Secret operations require HTTPS or loopback HTTP.
+ Expose SSH Kerberos keytab, principal and ticket refresh settings.
+ Add `collect ... --from eos:RUNNER` and EOS transfer sources for retrieving
  cached stageout into Yuki or an SSH runner.
+ Accept multiple task/directory paths in `submit`, including their dependencies
  in one workflow, in both standalone and interactive CLIs.
+ Add a positive `submit --cores N` workflow budget for native, SSH and IHEP
  runners. REANA rejects this option; existing workflow reuse is unchanged.
+ Run SSH APD tasks through CVMFS lb-conda, with optional ap_config.lb_conda
  release selection, while preserving token-file injection and dataList output.
+ Discover a local Yuki service's published port on each connection, falling
  back to the configured project endpoint when no valid local port is available.
+ Include Python 3.9 resource traversal and CI/lint compatibility fixes made
  after the previous release preparation.

Upgrade CelebiChrono and Yuki together to 1.1.3b1 and restart the Yuki HTTP service
and workers. See docs/secrets.rst for credential storage and supported backends.
This source release does not itself publish packages or deploy services.
